---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/SectionLabel.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Will It Fit Terms of Use"
  description="Will It Fit's terms of use: what the one-time unlock buys, what the app's measurements are and are not, and the limits of relying on them."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-8 py-section">
      <SectionLabel label="will it fit · terms of use" />
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-page-h1 text-text-primary max-w-prose">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-card-body text-text-secondary max-w-prose">
        Last updated: August 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-8 section-divider"></div>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-8 py-section max-w-prose space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">The agreement</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Will It Fit is an iOS app published by Stewart Burton. By downloading or using it you
          agree to these terms. The app is also covered by Apple's Licensed Application End User
          License Agreement, which applies in addition to this page and can be read at
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" class="text-accent hover:underline">apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula</a>.
          Where the two ever conflict, Apple's standard EULA wins.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">What the app does</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Will It Fit measures a space and an object with your iPhone's LiDAR sensor and tells you
          whether the object fits, including whether it can physically pass through the opening.
          It also compares measured dimensions against a bundled list of airline baggage limits
          and courier parcel sizes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Measurements are estimates, not guarantees</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          This is the important one. Every result the app gives you is an estimate produced from a
          sensor scan, and the accuracy of that scan depends on lighting, surface reflectivity, how
          thoroughly you scanned, and the hardware itself. The app tells you when its confidence is
          low, and it applies a safety margin before calling something a fit, but it cannot be
          right every time.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Do not rely on it alone for a decision that is expensive, irreversible, or unsafe. Check
          a tape measure before you buy the sofa, hire the van, or commit to a delivery. Verdicts
          marked as a tight squeeze deserve particular suspicion. Will It Fit is a tool that makes
          you better informed, not a warranty that something will fit.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Airline and courier size limits change without notice, and airlines enforce them
          inconsistently. The bundled figures are provided for convenience and are correct to the
          best of our knowledge at the time of the app release you have installed. Always confirm
          against your carrier's own published limits before you travel.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Purchases</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The app is free to download and includes a limited number of free fit checks so you can
          judge it before paying. The Lifetime Unlock is a single non-consumable in-app purchase of
          R159.99 in South Africa, US$7.99 (R143) in the United States, and the equivalent Apple
          price point in other territories. It is a one-time payment. There is no subscription, no
          renewal, and no recurring charge of any kind.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The unlock removes the free-check limit and enables unlimited saved spaces, Best Fit
          ranking, Pack Check, the AR preview, and share cards without a watermark. It is tied to
          your Apple Account, so it restores on your other devices and after a reinstall using the
          Restore Purchases option in Settings.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Payment is taken by Apple, not by us. Refunds are handled by Apple under its own terms,
          which you can request at
          <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
          We cannot issue a refund directly, though we would still like to hear from you if
          something went wrong.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Device requirements</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Scanning requires an iPhone with a LiDAR sensor. On other devices the app still works
          using typed or tap-measured dimensions, but it cannot scan, and the accuracy of a
          tap-measured dimension is lower. This is a hardware limit, not a licensing one, and it is
          stated on the App Store listing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Don't decompile, reverse-engineer, or redistribute the app, and don't try to circumvent
          the purchase mechanism. Use it lawfully, and respect other people's privacy when pointing
          a camera at things.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The app is provided as-is. To the fullest extent permitted by law, the developer is not
          liable for any loss, damage, cost, or wasted journey arising from a measurement being
          wrong or a verdict being relied upon, including damage to an item or a vehicle during an
          attempt to fit something. Nothing in these terms limits any liability that cannot legally
          be limited, and nothing here affects your statutory consumer rights under the South
          African Consumer Protection Act or the equivalent law where you live.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The app collects no data and makes no network requests of its own. Full detail on the
          <a href="/willitfit/privacy" class="text-accent hover:underline">privacy policy</a> page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          If these terms change, the update will be posted on this page with a new "last updated"
          date above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:ai@stewart-burton.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">ai@stewart-burton.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
